{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1033104-werewolves-are-all-liz-lemon","id":1033104,"title":"Werewolves are all Liz Lemon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-16T19:54:34-08:00","id":1033104,"title":"Werewolves are all Liz Lemon","content":"<a href=\"http://littleblessedvillain.tumblr.com/post/155966295905/werewolves-are-all-liz-lemon\" target=\"_blank\">Reposted from my tumblr</a>:<br /> <br /> (spoilers for large images)<br /> <span style=\"color:#A1A1A1\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Not in a literal sense, but in a narrative one. Liz\u2019s character arc is about finding a work/life balance. The core internal struggle of the Uratha in Werewolf: The Forsaken (especially 2nd Edition) is about finding a balance between their Flesh sides and their Spirit sides. There\u2019s also some angsty stuff about how they can never really truly belong anywhere because choosing to focus on one of their sides leads to destruction and internal chaos, but 30 Rock is a comedy TV show and Werewolf is a horror game so not everything\u2019s going to sync up perfectly.<br /> </span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://68.media.tumblr.com/e664e0f7a91773c8d57769dbb8a3cdc2/tumblr_inline_ojwc06dWe61rzfgwx_500.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> <span style=\"color:#A1A1A1\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>Fun note, in looking for images for this post I found a lot more werewolves in 30 Rock than I expected, or remembered.<br /> </i></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#A1A1A1\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Let\u2019s start with a brief explanation of Harmony and why it\u2019s important to Werewolf. Like most of the other * of Darkness games, Werewolf has a stat that tracks the player characters\u2019 behavior. In Werewolf, this stat is Harmony, and it represents how balanced the character is. In 2nd Edition, having a high Harmony means the character is too attuned to their Flesh side, and they find shapeshifting difficult, and painful, and Rage more easily (leading to dead parents, ruined relationships, etc\u2026), while having a low Harmony means the character is too attuned to their Spirit side, and they find shapeshifting too easy (it happens even if they don\u2019t want it to), they have to abide by bizarre spiritual behaviors, and they Rage more easily. You wanna keep your Harmony in the middle. Characters also have two Touchstones, which are NPCs, places, or ideologies that serve as a focus for the Flesh or Spirit.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#A1A1A1\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Liz Lemon has these same problems. Her Spirit side is her job as the head writer of TGS, a Saturday Night Live-style comedy show on NBC. Her Spirit Touchstone is the show itself. Her Flesh side is her desire to have a family. Most of her problems stem from the fact that she doesn\u2019t have a stable Flesh touchstone until she meets Criss. The best part of this is that she suffers a lot of the same problems as a low-Harmony werewolf: strange, obsessive behaviors; prone to blacking out and making terrible decisions; and adopting strange eating habits.</span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://68.media.tumblr.com/63adca55efd0538a5fd8b996efda689e/tumblr_inline_ojwc0hoxGE1rzfgwx_500.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> <span style=\"color:#A1A1A1\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>Basically this, all the time. It\u2019s not good for her health. Also, she kidnaps babies</i></span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#A1A1A1\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><br /> The point of all of this is that werewolves, like Liz Lemon, are the splat about Having it All<sup>TM</sup>. Liz\u2019s arc finishes when she\u2019s at Harmony 5: she\u2019s married and has kids but she\u2019s also still a comedy writer at NBC. Obviously she has to make compromises to maintain that Harmony, but such is life.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#A1A1A1\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">A good Werewolf: The Forsaken game is a juggling act between the extremes of the characters\u2019 natures. Whether they\u2019re maintaining a healthy balance or diving into the deep end of Harmony, playing out those moments is how you find the game\u2019s heart. The Storyteller and players need to include the little mundane moments of their characters\u2019 lives and showcase the compromises the werewolves need to make. Show them abandoning a Sacred Hunt to attend their son\u2019s dance recital. Show them missing a date to mediate a dispute between the local packs and spirit court. Show them miss picking up their newly-adopted kids to try and save the pack\u2019s sketch comedy TV show. And then the pack comes together to make sure that they can go meet their kids instead.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#A1A1A1\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Werewolf, like all Chronicles of Darkness games, is about the struggle. But remember, not all struggles have to be monumental.</span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://68.media.tumblr.com/51ba3988e8b7ca984d73750fed5cbea3/tumblr_inline_ojwc0yLeKP1rzfgwx_500.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> <span style=\"color:#A1A1A1\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>I just love this picture and want to include it in every blog I write forever. Go check out @heymonster<br /> </i></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T20:14:32-08:00","id":1033111,"title":"","content":"Jack's a great Ivory Claw.<br /> <br /> Would Kenneth be a Fire-Touched?<br /> <br /> I like your take on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T20:22:01-08:00","id":1033113,"title":"","content":"I have Jack as their totem actually. He &quot;belongs&quot; to a court of executives and the super rich. Which makes Tracy the Ithaeur since he's closer to that world than anybody else. Liz herself is an Elodoth. Kenneth is clearly a Lune. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I admit, I haven't put much thought into tribes, seeing them as where the metaphor starts to break down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T20:27:06-08:00","id":1033115,"title":"","content":"Naturally naturally. In going with the work = spirit angle, I was conflating workaholics like Kenneth and Jack with the more spiritually-inclined. Plus like the Ivory Claws, Jack moves 'among the wealthy and powerful.'<br /> <br /> My own metaphor falls apart when the other characters get involved. Though I'd probably have Tracy as a Ithaeur too.<br /> <br /> I suppose Dennis would be a great Bale Hound for a family-friendly version of Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T06:38:33-08:00","id":1033317,"title":"","content":"Dennis as a Bale Hound is probably the best comparison I've heard so far.<br /> <br /> Also, I want to revise my thoughts on Kenneth, because he actually fits really well as 3 different things: I can see him as a Lune, Beast, or <i>idigam</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T12:04:20-08:00","id":1033527,"title":"","content":"You do him a disservice, gentlefolk! Kenneth is simply Kenneth, the mysterious associate who may or may not be immortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T17:37:46-08:00","id":1035549,"title":"","content":"Kenneth is a Sleeper, unaware that his office-mates are actually werewolves.<br /> <br /> He has 5-dots of that merit that lets him willfully ignore the supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","